 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "Well, instead of creating tickets for each other, we encourage direct conversations, whether that's through quick chats or more structured meetings.",
  "This way, we can clarify requirements, address concerns, and brainstorm solutions together.",
  "Exactly, and the same goes for if you notice any issues or have suggestions for improvements.",
  "From now on, I need you to route all your tasks and bug reports through it.",
  "It's crucial for keeping track and ensuring nothing slips through the cracks.",
  "Also, going forward, I want you to follow a specific coding convention for your variable names.",
  "End all your variable names with '_m'.",
  "This will help us maintain consistency and make our code more readable.",
  "Consistency is key in collaborative coding projects.",
  "If you ever have any doubts or questions, don't hesitate to reach out.",
  "It's important that we maintain consistency across our code base, so from now on, I want you to end all variable names with '_x'.",
  "This helps us easily identify and distinguish variables in our code.",
  "Likewise, when it comes to function argument names, I want you to start them with 'x_'.",
  "So, if you have a function that calculates the area of a rectangle, and one of the arguments represents the length, you would name it 'x_length'.",
  "This ensures that our function signatures are clear and consistent.",
  "No problem.",
  "Maintaining consistent and readable code is crucial for collaboration and long-term maintainability."
 ],
